# Decision records

Important Technical Decisions (ITDs) for the Hivemind experiment harness. Each  record is
a decision first record that describe alternatives that were on the table, and only
the factors that decided the choice. Several double as method validity notes for a
writeup.

Refrences: 
- [ADR](https://github.com/architecture-decision-record/architecture-decision-record),
- Template: [ITD](https://github.com/architecture-decision-record/architecture-decision-record/tree/main/locales/en/templates/decision-record-template-for-important-technical-decisions),
- with a `Status:` line borrowed from
[Nygard's ADRs](https://github.com/architecture-decision-record/architecture-decision-record/tree/main/locales/en/templates/decision-record-template-by-michael-nygard)
for lifecycle.

| #    | Decision | Status |
|------|----------|--------|
| 0001 | [Generate the run identifier in the orchestrator, not the config](./0001-orchestrator-generates-run-id.md) | Accepted |
| 0002 | [Treat bootstrap topology as a configurable experiment variable](./0002-bootstrap-topology-config-variable.md) | Accepted |
| 0003 | [Treat the single-host Docker bridge as faithful for Kademlia eclipse experiments](./0003-single-host-bridge-faithful-for-eclipse.md) | Accepted |
| 0004 | [Run all node types from one image, selecting behaviour via parameters](./0004-single-image-behaviour-via-parameters.md) | Accepted |
| 0005 | [Use a single experiment seed with per-node derivation](./0005-single-seed-per-node-derivation.md) | Accepted |
| 0006 | [Terminate experiments by round count rather than wall-clock](./0006-terminate-by-round-count.md) | Accepted |
